  "worked_solution": "If $A\u2286B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $C\u2286Z$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every complex is an integer number. For example, we have $2\\text{i}\\in C$ but $2\\text{i}\\notin Z.$",
